 {path:'/guides/custom-website-or-template/',title:'Custom website or template? Start with the job.',category:'Websites',image:'custom-or-template',alt:'Two fictional website concepts comparing a template layout with a custom editorial direction',description:'Compare a custom website and a template around content, editing, accessibility, ongoing cost and the customer journey for a small service business.',minutes:5,fallback:'/services/web-design/'},
 {path:'/guides/website-care-versus-seo/',title:'Website care, monthly SEO or growth: what are you paying for?',category:'Planning',image:'care-versus-seo',diagram:true,imageHeight:520,alt:'Two work lanes: keep the site working and improve the search decision. Both lead to verifying and recording the change.',description:'Compare website maintenance and SEO by the problem, agreed task and verification. Includes a decision worksheet, current studio plan references and an owned change record.',minutes:6,fallback:'/services/website-care/',datePublished:'2026-10-15'},
 {path:'/guides/website-audit-checklist/',title:'A website audit checklist you can actually use',category:'Websites',image:'audit-checklist',diagram:true,imageHeight:660,alt:'Audit sequence: question, evidence, priority, small agreed fix, retest and dated record. Missing access is recorded and obtained before dependent checks continue.',description:'Start a small business website audit with a failing visitor task. Download an actionable checklist and inspect two documented fixes, with access and testing limits made clear.',minutes:7,fallback:'/services/website-audit/',datePublished:'2026-10-15'},
 {path:'/guides/website-repair-or-redesign/',title:'Repair or redesign your website? Choose the smallest useful change.',category:'Planning',image:'repair-or-redesign',diagram:true,imageHeight:850,diagramCaption:'Process diagram: first confirm the visitor task and access. Keep a useful site when the task works. If a supported contained correction and its retest are known, fix and verify it. Otherwise diagnose the scope: rework the current content or structure where it can support the requirements, or assess a rebuild. Missing access pauses the dependent decision; no branch promises a price or outcome.',alt:'Decision tree for keeping, correcting, reworking or rebuilding a website, with a separate needs-access branch before the decision.',description:'For Buffalo and Erie County small businesses deciding whether an existing website needs a contained fix, broader rework or a rebuild. Includes owned examples and a decision worksheet.',minutes:6,fallback:'/services/website-audit/',datePublished:'2026-10-15'}
